<main id="main">
<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/snowy-house.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/snowy-house-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/snowy-house.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="683" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.18"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/service-locations/">Locations</a></li><li aria-current="page">Hagerstown</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker">Western Maryland · Washington County</p><h1>Hagerstown Insurance Appraiser for Snow, Hail and Wind Claims</h1><p class="lede">Hagerstown gets more snow and stronger thunderstorms than the Bay side of the state, and its older brick homes add their own complications. As an insurance appraiser in Hagerstown, MD, we help owners get those claims priced correctly.</p><div class="btns"><a class="btn brass" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn ghost-l" href="/start-a-claim-review/">Request a free review</a></div><dl class="ph-facts"><div><dt>County</dt><dd>Washington County</dd></div><div><dt>Region</dt><dd>Western Maryland</dd></div><div><dt>Inspections</dt><dd>On site</dd></div></dl></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose"><div class="localcard"><div><h2 class="lc-h">Local claim risks</h2><ul class="chips"><li>Heavy snow and ice dams</li><li>Hail</li><li>Frozen pipes</li><li>Creek flooding</li><li>Wind</li></ul></div><div><h2 class="lc-h">Storms on record</h2><ul class="dots"><li>Tropical Storm Agnes, 1972</li><li>January 1996 flood</li><li>February 2010 blizzards</li><li>June 2012 derecho</li></ul></div><div class="full"><h2 class="lc-h">Housing mix</h2><p>Older brick rowhouses and detached homes downtown, mid-century houses on the city’s edges, and newer subdivisions and farmhouses across Washington County.</p><p class="hoods"><b>Neighborhoods &amp; nearby:</b> Downtown Hagerstown, Halfway, Funkstown, Williamsport, Smithsburg, Boonsboro, Maugansville</p></div></div><h2>Western Maryland weather at the crossroads</h2>
<p>Hagerstown sits in the Great Valley at the meeting point of I-70 and I-81, and it is the county seat of Washington County. Its weather leans toward the west: more snow than the Bay counties, frequent spring and summer thunderstorms with hail, and creek flooding along Antietam and Conococheague Creeks. An insurance appraiser in Hagerstown, MD sees all of these show up in claims, often on homes that are a century old.</p>
<h2>Snow, ice dams and frozen pipes</h2>
<p>The February 2010 blizzards buried Washington County and loaded roofs well beyond their normal weight. Ice dams form along the eaves of older homes with limited attic insulation, and meltwater backs up under shingles into ceilings and walls. Frozen pipes are another winter loss, especially in older houses with plumbing on exterior walls. Common disputes include:</p>
<ul>
<li>Ice-dam leaks treated as maintenance problems instead of sudden water damage</li>
<li>Ceiling patches priced without accounting for wet insulation or framing</li>
<li>Frozen pipe claims questioned over whether heat was maintained</li>
<li>Snow-load damage to porches, carports and outbuildings left off the estimate</li>
</ul>
<p>Our <a href="/property-claim-services/snow-ice-dam-freeze-appraisal/">snow, ice dam and freeze appraisal</a> page explains how winter losses are usually documented.</p>
<h2>Floods and storms in local memory</h2>
<p>Tropical Storm Agnes in 1972 flooded rivers and creeks across Maryland, and the January 1996 flood – driven by rapid snowmelt and rain – hit Western Maryland hard. Flooding from streams and rivers is generally excluded from homeowners policies and requires separate flood coverage. The June 2012 derecho also caused wind and tree damage in Washington County. Wind and hail are usually covered, while rising water is not, so separating the causes is important.</p>
<h2>Communities around Hagerstown we serve</h2>
<p>We inspect in downtown Hagerstown and in Halfway, Funkstown, Williamsport, Smithsburg, Boonsboro and Maugansville. Farm properties in the county raise additional questions about barns, outbuildings and other structures coverage.</p>
<p>Downtown Hagerstown’s older brick homes often have plaster walls, slate or metal roofs and original wood trim. When winter water damage reaches these interiors, carriers may price drywall and modern trim instead of plaster and period millwork. Matching older materials takes more time and skill, and those costs belong in the estimate.</p><p>Hail is also common in the Great Valley during spring and summer storms. Newer subdivisions around Hagerstown, with architectural shingles and vinyl siding, can show widespread damage that is easy to undercount if only one slope or elevation is inspected.</p>
<h2>Advice for Washington County owners</h2>
<p>After a snowstorm, photograph roof snow depth and any icicles or ice ridges along the eaves before they melt. Keep heating bills or thermostat records if you have a frozen pipe claim, since they help show the home was heated. After hail, photograph dents on gutters, vents and car hoods as supporting evidence.</p>
<p>Maryland Insurance Appraiser can review your carrier’s estimate and, if the amount is disputed, represent you through the appraisal clause in your policy.</p><h2>Services for Hagerstown property owners</h2><p>Every service is available in Hagerstown and the rest of Washington County, including:</p><ul class="cols2"><li><a href="/property-claim-services/appraisal-demand-representation/">Appraisal Demand Representation</a></li><li><a href="/property-claim-services/home-insurance-appraisal/">Home Insurance Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-claim-services/commercial-hoa-appraisal/">Commercial &amp; HOA Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-claim-services/roof-hail-damage-appraisal/">Roof &amp; Hail Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-claim-services/windstorm-tornado-appraisal/">Windstorm &amp; Tornado Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-claim-services/hurricane-noreaster-appraisal/">Hurricane &amp; Nor’easter Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-claim-services/water-damage-appraisal/">Water Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-claim-services/fire-smoke-damage-appraisal/">Fire &amp; Smoke Damage Appraisal</a></li></ul>
<h2>Hagerstown claim questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Is ice dam damage covered in Hagerstown?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>Many homeowners policies cover sudden interior water damage from ice dams, though the ice dam itself and long-term leaks may be excluded. Policy wording varies, so check the water damage and exclusions sections.</p></div></details><details><summary>My pipes froze while I was away. Will my claim be paid?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>Policies often require that you maintain heat or drain the system when a home is unoccupied. If you kept heat on, keep proof such as utility bills. If the carrier denies the claim on this basis, a Maryland attorney can review the wording.</p></div></details></div><h2>Nearby service areas</h2><div class="rel"><a href="/service-locations/frederick/"><small>Nearby</small><span>Frederick</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a href="/service-locations/cumberland/"><small>Nearby</small><span>Cumberland</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a href="/service-locations/rockville/"><small>Nearby</small><span>Rockville</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></article><aside class="side"><div class="side-in"><div class="box box-call"><h2 class="box-h">Talk to an appraiser</h2><p>A free first conversation about your estimate — and a straight answer on whether appraisal fits.</p><a class="box-tel" href="tel:+